IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `je21-nouns`

-- je21-art17-18-official-versions: Articles 17 and 18 of the Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021 (L.8/2021):
-- 17 Official versions of legislation, 18 Statute Law Revision Regulations.
--
-- The page banner of a deposited source may say that a text is an official version; the model does not rely on it.
-- The facts that Article 17 turns on are inputs, stated by the reader about the text in front of them.
--
-- Article 17(6) lets the States vary the requirements of Article 17(2) by Regulations.
-- The Table of Legislation History in the endnotes records no such Regulations, so the model applies Article 17(2) as deposited.
--
-- L11 (Article 17(2) is "an official version if", not "only if") is a fork: see the nouns module and NOTES.md.

§ `Article 17 -- Official versions of legislation`

§§ `17(1) and (2) Which texts are official versions`

-- Answers: does Article 17(1) or (2) make this text an official version of the legislation?
-- All as-enacted legislation is one (17(1)).
-- Consolidated legislation, which includes revised legislation (12(4)), is one if it is Jersey legislation, it contains the statement that it is an official version issued under the authority of the Law,
-- and either it is the electronic version displayed under the authority of the Principal Legislative Drafter (or an unaltered printed or downloaded copy of that) or it is a printed version issued by or on behalf of the Principal Legislative Drafter (17(2)).
-- TRUE means the Article makes it an official version.
-- FALSE means the Article does not; whether the Law says it is then not an official version is fork L11.
-- src:167 | (1) All as-enacted legislation is an official version of the legislation.
-- src:168 | (2) Any consolidated legislation that is Jersey legislation is an official version if it contains a statement that it is an official version of the legislation issued under the authority of this Law and –
-- src:169 | (a) it is an electronic version of the legislation displayed on a website under the authority of the Principal Legislative Drafter (or a printed or downloaded version of that legislation without any alteration to its text or format); or
-- src:170 | (b) it is a printed version of the legislation issued by or on behalf of the Principal Legislative Drafter.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 17(1) and (2) (src:167-170)
GIVEN text IS A `Facts about a text`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 17(1) and (2): the text is made an official version` text MEANS
    IF text's `its kind` EQUALS `as-enacted legislation`
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE     text's `it is Jersey legislation`
         AND text's `it contains a statement that it is an official version of the legislation issued under the authority of the Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021`
         AND (    text's `it is an electronic version displayed on a website under the authority of the Principal Legislative Drafter, or a printed or downloaded copy of that without any alteration to its text or format`
              OR  text's `it is a printed version issued by or on behalf of the Principal Legislative Drafter`)

-- Answers: is this text an official version of the legislation?
-- When Article 17(1) and (2) make it one, yes.
-- When they do not: on the first reading of L11 it is not one, and on the second the Law does not say, and the model refuses.
-- src:167 | (1) All as-enacted legislation is an official version of the legislation.
-- src:168 | (2) Any consolidated legislation that is Jersey legislation is an official version if it contains a statement that it is an official version of the legislation issued under the authority of this Law and –
-- src:169 | (a) it is an electronic version of the legislation displayed on a website under the authority of the Principal Legislative Drafter (or a printed or downloaded version of that legislation without any alteration to its text or format); or
-- src:170 | (b) it is a printed version of the legislation issued by or on behalf of the Principal Legislative Drafter.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 17(1) and (2) (src:167-170)
GIVEN text IS A `Facts about a text`
      reading IS A `Reading L11 of whether Article 17(2) is the only route to an official version of consolidated legislation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 17(1) and (2): the text is an official version` text reading MEANS
    IF `Article 17(1) and (2): the text is made an official version` text
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE CONSIDER reading
         WHEN `Article 17(2) is the only route, so consolidated legislation that does not meet it is not an official version` THEN FALSE
         WHEN `Article 17(2) is a sufficient route, so whether other consolidated legislation is an official version is not answered`
             THEN REFUSE "Article 17(2) says consolidated legislation that meets its conditions is an official version, and the Law does not say whether other consolidated legislation is one"

§§ `17(3) and (4) What an official version is taken to set out`

-- Answers: is the official version of this as-enacted legislation taken to set out the text of the legislation correctly?
-- It is, and paragraph (3), unlike paragraph (4), has no "unless the contrary is shown" in it, so the model gives no input for a contrary showing.
-- Anything that is not as-enacted legislation is outside the paragraph, and the model refuses.
-- src:171 | (3) An official version of as-enacted legislation is taken to set out correctly the text of the legislation.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 17(3) (src:171)
GIVEN text IS A `Facts about a text`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 17(3): the official version is taken to set out the text of the as-enacted legislation correctly` text MEANS
    IF text's `its kind` EQUALS `as-enacted legislation`
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE REFUSE "Article 17(3) speaks of an official version of as-enacted legislation, and this text is not as-enacted legislation"

-- Answers: is the official version of this consolidated legislation taken to set out the legislation correctly, as at the date on which it is stated to be consolidated?
-- It is, unless the contrary is shown.
-- The presumption is as at that date only, and the question must be about that date.
-- The paragraph is "Subject to Article 15(8)", which gives the changes made by a revision effect as if made by amendment; the paragraph gives no further rule for a conflict and the model adds none.
-- FALSE means the contrary is shown, so the text is not taken to set the legislation out correctly.
-- A text that is not an official version of consolidated legislation is outside the paragraph, and the model refuses.
-- src:172 | (4) Subject to Article 15(8) (changes made by revision have effect as if effected by amendment), an official version of consolidated legislation, unless the contrary is shown, is taken to set out correctly, as at the date on which it is stated to be consolidated, the legislation as enacted and including any current amendments to it, or revisions of it.[4]
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 17(4) (src:172)
GIVEN text IS A `Facts about a text`
      `the contrary is shown` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the question is about the legislation as at the date on which the text is stated to be consolidated` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 17(4): the official version is taken to set out the consolidated legislation correctly` text `the contrary is shown` `the question is about the legislation as at the date on which the text is stated to be consolidated` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF text's `its kind` EQUALS `as-enacted legislation`
            THEN REFUSE "Article 17(4) speaks of an official version of consolidated legislation, and this text is as-enacted legislation, which Article 17(3) deals with"
        IF NOT `Article 17(1) and (2): the text is made an official version` text
            THEN REFUSE "Article 17(4) speaks of an official version of consolidated legislation, and Article 17(2) does not make this text one"
        IF NOT `the question is about the legislation as at the date on which the text is stated to be consolidated`
            THEN REFUSE "Article 17(4) speaks only of the legislation as at the date on which the text is stated to be consolidated, and the Law does not say what the text is taken to set out for any other date"
        OTHERWISE NOT `the contrary is shown`

§§ `17(5) Admissibility and judicial notice`

-- Answers: is this text admissible in evidence in any proceedings?
-- An official version of legislation is.
-- A text that is not an official version is outside the paragraph, and the model refuses.
-- src:173 | (5) An official version of legislation is admissible in evidence in any proceedings and a court or person acting judicially must take judicial notice of any official version of legislation.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 17(5) (src:173)
GIVEN text IS A `Facts about a text`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 17(5): the text is admissible in evidence in any proceedings` text MEANS
    IF `Article 17(1) and (2): the text is made an official version` text
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE REFUSE "Article 17(5) speaks of an official version of legislation, and Article 17(1) and (2) do not make this text one; the Law does not say whether any other text is admissible"

-- Answers: must a court or person acting judicially take judicial notice of this text?
-- Of any official version of legislation, it must.
-- A text that is not an official version is outside the paragraph, and the model refuses.
-- src:173 | (5) An official version of legislation is admissible in evidence in any proceedings and a court or person acting judicially must take judicial notice of any official version of legislation.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 17(5) (src:173)
GIVEN text IS A `Facts about a text`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 17(5): a court or person acting judicially must take judicial notice of the text` text MEANS
    IF `Article 17(1) and (2): the text is made an official version` text
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE REFUSE "Article 17(5) speaks of an official version of legislation, and Article 17(1) and (2) do not make this text one; the Law does not say whether a court must take notice of any other text"

§ `Article 18 -- Statute Law Revision Regulations`

§§ `18(1) and (2) What the Regulations may amend, and for what`

-- Answers: may Statute Law Revision Regulations amend this legislation in this way?
-- They may amend any Jersey legislation using the powers set out in paragraph (2), Article 14 or Schedule 1.
-- The power in paragraph (2) is to make amendments necessary or desirable to clarify an ambiguity, or to reconcile inconsistencies between provisions of the legislation or with provisions of other Jersey legislation.
-- Whether the amendment is necessary or desirable for that purpose is a judgement and is the ground the reader states.
-- FALSE means Article 18(1) and (2) do not give the power.
-- src:176 | (1) The States may by Regulations amend any Jersey legislation using the powers set out in paragraph (2), Article 14 or Schedule 1.
-- src:177 | (2) The power is to make such amendments as are necessary or desirable to –
-- src:178 | (a) clarify any ambiguity in the legislation; or
-- src:179 | (b) reconcile inconsistencies between different provisions of the legislation or between any of its provisions and provisions of any other Jersey legislation.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 18(1) and (2) (src:176-179)
GIVEN `the legislation to be amended is Jersey legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      ground IS A `Ground of an amendment under Article 18`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 18(1) and (2): Statute Law Revision Regulations may make the amendment` `the legislation to be amended is Jersey legislation` ground MEANS
        `the legislation to be amended is Jersey legislation`
    AND CONSIDER ground
        WHEN `the amendment is necessary or desirable to clarify an ambiguity in the legislation` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `the amendment is necessary or desirable to reconcile inconsistencies between different provisions of the legislation, or between any of its provisions and provisions of any other Jersey legislation` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `the amendment uses a power set out in Article 14` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `the amendment uses a power set out in Schedule 1` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `the amendment rests on none of these` THEN FALSE

§§ `18(3) Amendments lodged to the proposition`

-- Answers: does Article 18(3) leave this amendment free to be lodged?
-- Where a proposition is lodged in respect of Regulations to be made under Article 18, no amendment may be lodged that in the opinion of the Bailiff would alter the effect of any legislation,
-- unless it is within the scope of paragraph (1) or (2); the amendment is within that scope when Article 18(1) and (2) give the power to make it.
-- "in the opinion of the Bailiff" is read as governing the whole of "would alter the effect of any legislation", and not the "unless" limb, which is a matter of fact about the amendment.
-- TRUE means paragraph (3) does not bar it; whether it may be lodged under other rules is not answered here.
-- FALSE means paragraph (3) bars it.
-- Paragraph (3) bars amendments to a proposition for Regulations under Article 18 and to no other, so for any other proposition it does not bar the amendment and the answer is TRUE.
-- The question is what the paragraph decides: a bar, and only that bar. It does not say that any other proposition's amendment may be lodged.
-- src:180 | (3) Where a proposition is lodged in respect of Regulations to be made under this Article no amendment may be lodged that, in the opinion of the Bailiff, would alter the effect of any legislation unless it is within the scope of paragraphs (1) or (2).
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 18(3) (src:180)
GIVEN `the proposition is for Regulations to be made under Article 18` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in the opinion of the Bailiff the amendment would alter the effect of legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the legislation the amendment would amend is Jersey legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      ground IS A `Ground of an amendment under Article 18`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 18(3): the amendment is not barred from being lodged` `the proposition is for Regulations to be made under Article 18` `in the opinion of the Bailiff the amendment would alter the effect of legislation` `the legislation the amendment would amend is Jersey legislation` ground MEANS
    IF `the proposition is for Regulations to be made under Article 18`
    THEN     NOT `in the opinion of the Bailiff the amendment would alter the effect of legislation`
         OR  `Article 18(1) and (2): Statute Law Revision Regulations may make the amendment` `the legislation the amendment would amend is Jersey legislation` ground
    ELSE TRUE

§§ `18(4) What else the Regulations may contain`

-- Answers: may Statute Law Revision Regulations make this provision?
-- Subject to the Article, the Regulations may make any provision that could be made by a Law.
-- The limits the Article puts on the Regulations are those of paragraphs (1) and (2) on the amendments they make; a provision that amends nothing meets them vacuously.
-- FALSE means the Article's own limit says no: an amendment the provision makes is not one paragraphs (1) and (2) give the power to make.
-- A provision that a Law could not make is given no power by this paragraph, and the Law says nothing else about it, so the model refuses.
-- The limit is checked first: a provision that fails it is FALSE whether or not a Law could make it.
-- src:181 | (4) Subject to this Article, the Regulations may make any provision that could be made by a Law.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 18(4) (src:181)
GIVEN `a Law could make the provision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `any amendment the provision makes is one Article 18(1) and (2) give the power to make` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 18(4): Statute Law Revision Regulations may make the provision` `a Law could make the provision` `any amendment the provision makes is one Article 18(1) and (2) give the power to make` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `any amendment the provision makes is one Article 18(1) and (2) give the power to make` THEN FALSE
        IF NOT `a Law could make the provision`
            THEN REFUSE "Article 18(4) lets Statute Law Revision Regulations make any provision that could be made by a Law, and the Law does not say whether they may make a provision that a Law could not"
        OTHERWISE TRUE
